Temporary migration shim. Delete it once no Workload that held quota under
patch release p0.6.x or earlier remains.

Those releases set every Ray worker group's minCount to its minReplicas.
Kueue compares minCount when it checks that a job still matches its Workload,
so after an upgrade every running RayCluster, RayJob, and RayService they
admitted stops matching, and Kueue deletes its Workload and suspends it. The
Ray integrations now ignore minCount in that check while the Workload holds
quota; once the quota is released, Kueue replaces the Workload's PodSets with
the job's as usual.

